---
import ContentLayout from "../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { HOME } from "../../utils/breadcrumbs";
const analytics = Boolean(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN);
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What DataDank does and does not collect: no accounts, no forms and no advertising trackers. Your study progress stays in your own browser."
  crumbs={[HOME, { label: "Privacy" }]}
  eyebrow="Legal"
  indexable
>
  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <p>
        There are no accounts, no comments and no forms on this site. We do not sell or share
        personal data. If advertising is switched on in future, this page will name the provider and
        explain its cookies first.
      </p>
      <h2>Information stored on your device</h2>
      <p>
        Some preferences and your learning progress are saved in your browser’s local storage, on
        your device only:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <code>dch-theme</code>: your light or dark theme choice.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>dch-sidebar</code>: whether you hid the course menu.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>dch-progress-v1</code>: pages you have opened, items you marked as done, and the
          last lesson you visited, so the site can show your progress and a “continue” link.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>dch-planner-v1</code>: the 90-day plan days and study topics you ticked, and the
          optional start date you set.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This information is never sent to us or anyone else. It stays in this browser, does not
        follow you to other devices, and is removed if you clear this site’s data. You can also
        clear your progress with the “Reset” link in the “Your progress” panel on the home page.
      </p>
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      {analytics ? (
        <p>
          This site uses Cloudflare Web Analytics for aggregate page-view and performance
          statistics. It is described by Cloudflare as privacy-first and does not use cookies or
          collect personal data for cross-site tracking. We do not record sessions or build profiles
          of individual visitors.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>
          This deployment does not currently load any analytics script. If aggregate analytics are
          enabled later, this page will be updated to name the tool before it is switched on.
        </p>
      )}
      <h2>Server logs</h2>
      <p>
        Our hosting provider, Cloudflare, processes requests to deliver the site and may keep
        standard technical logs such as IP address and user agent for security and reliability. See
        Cloudflare’s own privacy documentation for details.
      </p>
      <h2>Search</h2>
      <p>
        Search runs entirely in your browser against a static index. Your search terms are not sent
        to a server.
      </p>
      <h2>Emailing us</h2>
      <p>
        If you email the address on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>, your message and email
        address are used only to reply and to fix what you reported. They are not added to a
        mailing list or shared.
      </p>
      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        Pages link to external sites such as vendor documentation. Those sites have their own
        privacy practices.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>
